tinyeop independently implements bounded linear/local cubic interpolation of
caller-supplied Earth-orientation and X/Y/s tables. TinyNadir contributions
are MIT licensed; no NumPy, Vallado or IERS implementation code/data archive
is included. Real Earth-orientation inputs are supplied by the application.

Independent numerical validation used NumPy 2.5.4 interp and Polynomial.fit
on synthetic fields. Reference packages/generators/raw results remain in
ignored .validation/; only numeric reference fixtures are retained in tests/data/.
The UT1-TAI storage convention avoids interpolating a leap-second jump;
see README.md for conversion to/from source DUT1 and query-time offsets.

References: https://www.iers.org/IERS/EN/DataProducts/EarthOrientationData/eop.html
            https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.interp.html
